# Shipwright site build environment.
#
# NAMES ONLY. Every value below is intentionally empty. Copy this file to
# `.env` for local builds and fill in real values there; `.env` is gitignored.
# The Netlify build environment is configured separately, out of band.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# SUPABASE_URL
#   Your Supabase project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#   Public by design. It appears in every page request.
#
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   The Supabase anon (publishable) key. It is designed to ship to a browser
#   and every read it performs is subject to row level security, so the
#   browser bundle is not a place a secret can hide.
#   Get it from Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API, or ask Rin.
#
# The service-role key is deliberately NOT listed here. It bypasses row level
# security and has no use in a static site build. Leaderboard writes are
# service-role only and run from a trusted backend, never from this repository.

SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
